    "notes": [
        "Chestnut Street divides the borough: garbage east of it is Tuesday & Friday, west of it Monday & Thursday. Chestnut St itself from Westfield Ave to Grant Ave is picked up Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday.",
        "Recycling is every Wednesday for the whole borough, alternating between commingled bottles, cans & plastics and commingled paper products.",
        "Put garbage, recycling and vegetative waste at the curb after 7 PM the evening before pickup; for Monday pickups, any time after 3 PM the afternoon before. Bulk waste goes out after 12 PM the day before.",
        "Use containers of 32 gallons or less with handles, 50 lb at most when full. No plastic bags for bulk waste, recycling or vegetative waste.",
        "Bulk: the last Friday of the month on the east side and the last Thursday on the west side (a few months differ, see the calendar), up to 3 items, for one- to four-family homes. Not bulk: carpeting, electronics, appliances, paint, ashes, dirt, tree trunks, stumps, branches, brush or leaves. Buildings with five or more units should call the DPW.",
        "E-waste, appliances (white goods) and extra \"a la carte\" bulk items are picked up for a fee by appointment: call the DPW at 908-245-7676 (for example couch $30, mattress or box spring $20, refrigerator $20, washer or dryer $10).",
        "Vegetative waste is picked up weekly from April 1 to December 31: Thursday on the east side, Friday on the west side. Free leaf bags are given out at the Borough Clerk's Office (110 E Westfield Ave, Mon-Fri 8:30 AM-4:30 PM) while they last.",
        "When garbage or vegetative waste falls on a holiday, it is picked up on the next scheduled day. Recycling moves to the next calendar day.",
        "The DPW does not take motor oil or any household hazardous waste: use Union County's programs (ucnj.org/recycling)."
    ],
